<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Klis Fortress</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Klis Fortress stands on a pass above Split in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, guarding the route from the Dalmatian coast to the interior. It was a seat of the early medieval Croatian dukes and kings, and in the 16th century the Uskoks defended it against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> until it fell in 1537. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> captured it in 1648.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/klis-fortress.jpg" alt="Klis Fortress" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Općina Klis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Klis_iz_zraka.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
